CLAUDE.md — Hilbert GQR Reasoning Unit Tests

0. Build this

Build a new, versioned test asset for Hilbert called:

Hilbert GQR Reasoning Unit Tests

A contrastive, source-backed test suite for Grocery, QSR & Retail growth reasoning.

This is NOT:

an eval platform

a customer report

a customer-facing diagnosis

a Hilbert replacement

a dashboard

an ICP tool

an ingestion product

a generic benchmark

It is a portable test pack that Hilbert's existing / future evaluation infrastructure can consume.

The core unit is not a standalone case.

It is a contrastive pair:

two real cases that look similar on the surface but differ in one important underlying mechanic.

The test asks:

Does Hilbert change its conclusion when the mechanic changes?

or:

Does Hilbert keep its conclusion stable when only irrelevant information changes?

That makes the suite much harder to game with generic cautious prose.

1. Why this is the final project

Hilbert already publicly says it:

detects metric shifts,

reasons over cohorts, products, channels and unit economics,

performs root-cause analysis and counterfactual reasoning,

analyzes promotions, pricing, loyalty, frequency and returns,

is building systematic evaluation pipelines.

Therefore do NOT build:

another reasoning engine,

another eval harness,

another customer-facing analysis surface.

The Growth Operator role specifically owns:

testing Hilbert on real GQR problems,

finding what it gets right,

finding what it misses,

finding where reasoning needs sharpening,

turning those findings into structured Product / Tech input.

This test suite is the operator-owned domain asset that feeds that process.

